The 2026 Worldwide Developers Conference will take place this week from June 8 through June 12, and like the last six years, it will be an online event, although select developers and students will be invited to Apple Park. To kick things off, Apple holds a keynote event on the Monday to announce new software, which is what makes it of interest to the general public.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/03/wwdc-2026-horizontal.jpg" alt="" width="1600" height="900" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1042153" /><br/>
During the keynote event on Monday, June 8, Apple is expected to unveil iOS 27, iPadOS 27, macOS 27, tvOS 27, watchOS 27, and visionOS 27. (The "27" represents the September 2026 to September 2027 release season.) <br/>
<br/>
